---
title: Concurrent Edits - Cross-Tab, Cross-Device & CLI Races
---
sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant TabA as Browser tab A<br/>(BoardProvider -><br/>useBoardPersistence.ts)
    participant Channel as BroadcastChannel<br/>board-sync:kv<br/>(same browser only)
    participant TabB as Browser tab B<br/>(BoardProvider + TaskEditModal,<br/>BoardView, BoardContext.tsx)
    participant BoardAPI@{ "type" : "boundary" } as /api/v1/board<br/>(sessionRoute)
    participant Events@{ "type" : "boundary" } as /api/v1/board/events<br/>(sessionRoute, SSE)
    participant KV@{ "type" : "database" } as Deno KV<br/>(lib/db/kv.ts)
    participant CliAPI@{ "type" : "boundary" } as /api/v1/tasks, /api/v1/rows<br/>(cliRoute)
    participant CLI as kanby CLI<br/>(cli/commands/task.ts, row.ts)

    Note over TabA,CLI: Two kinds of version are in play. Every board write sets ["board_rev", boardId], whose versionstamp is the board revision<br/>(the web app's If-Match, revRef). Each entity has its own versionstamp too (the CLI's If-Match, from GET /api/v1/tasks/:id or /rows/:id).<br/>A browser save is rejected if anything on the board changed. A CLI save is rejected only if that one task or row changed.
    Note over TabA,TabB: Each tab tracks savedRef (per-entity JSON the server has confirmed), revRef (the board revision it last saw),<br/>lastSyncedRef (the last board it received, so applying it isn't saved or broadcast back) and savePendingRef (an edit is on the 500ms autosave timer).

    rect rgba(38, 140, 240, 0.15)
        Note over User,CLI: 1. A task saved in tab A shows up in tab B through the BroadcastChannel
        User->>TabA: Save in TaskEditModal
        TabA->>TabA: saveTaskEdit -> POST /api/v1/validate/task (422 keeps the modal open)<br/>dispatch(TASK/SAVE_EDIT): task updated, editingTaskId = null, modal closed<br/>clearEditDraft(id), navigate("/dashboard")
        TabA->>TabA: autosave effect: savePendingRef = true, 500ms timer
        TabA->>TabA: timer fires: PATCH queued on saveChainRef
        TabA->>Channel: postMessage({rows, columns, tasks})<br/>(sent as soon as the timer fires, not after the PATCH succeeds)
        Channel->>TabB: onmessage(board)
        TabB->>TabB: closeStaleEdit(tasks) (no-op unless tab B has this task open, see 2)<br/>lastSyncedRef = board, savedRef = board (assumes tab A saved it)<br/>dispatch(BOARD/SYNC) -> rows/columns/tasks replaced, TaskCard re-renders
        TabB->>TabB: autosave effect: snapshot === lastSyncedRef -> no PATCH, no rebroadcast
        TabA->>BoardAPI: PATCH /api/v1/board {upserts: [task]} If-Match: revRef
        BoardAPI->>KV: applyBoardChanges(..., [revisionCheck(boardId, revRef)])<br/>atomic: check board_rev + set task + set board_rev
        KV-->>BoardAPI: ok
        BoardAPI-->>TabA: 200 + ETag -> revRef, savedRef updated
        KV-->>Events: board_rev changed
        Events-->>TabA: data: change -> refreshFromServer -> GET: matches savedRef, revRef = ETag
        Events-->>TabB: data: change -> refreshFromServer -> GET: matches savedRef, revRef = ETag
        Note over TabB: Until that SSE refetch, tab B's revRef is behind. A save from tab B in that window<br/>gets a 409 and merges without a notice (nothing collided).
        %% KNOWN RACE (unfixed): a broadcast silently drops the receiving tab's pending edit.
        %% Where: useBoardPersistence.ts, the BroadcastChannel effect's channel.onmessage.
        %% It applies BOARD/SYNC without checking savePendingRef, unlike refreshFromServer,
        %% which defers to the pending save via refreshQueuedRef.
        %% Effect: a change tab B made less than 500ms before the message (drag, checklist toggle,
        %% modal save) is replaced. The re-armed autosave timer then matches lastSyncedRef and skips
        %% the save. Tab B's change is lost with no notice.
        %% Not covered by a test yet.
        Note over Channel,TabB: RACE: the broadcast isn't held back for tab B's pending save (onmessage doesn't check savePendingRef).<br/>If tab B made a board change (drag, checklist toggle, its own modal save) less than 500ms before the message,<br/>BOARD/SYNC replaces it, the re-armed timer then matches lastSyncedRef, and tab B's change is dropped with no notice.
        Note over TabA,TabB: RACE: if tab A's PATCH then fails (409 or 4xx), tab B already shows tab A's version and holds it in savedRef.<br/>The next SSE refetch differs from savedRef, so BOARD/SYNC brings tab B back to what the server holds.
    end

    rect rgba(240, 163, 38, 0.15)
        Note over User,CLI: 2. Tab A saves a task that tab B has open, with unsaved edits, in its modal
        User->>TabB: open task T -> dispatch(TASK/OPEN_EDIT_MODAL)<br/>editingTaskId = T, editTaskDraft = copy of T, URL /dashboard/task/:shortId
        User->>TabB: type edits (held in editTaskDraft only: nothing is saved, tasks unchanged)
        User->>TabA: edit and Save task T (as in 1)
        TabA->>Channel: postMessage(board with the new T)
        Channel->>TabB: onmessage(board)
        TabB->>TabB: closeStaleEdit(tasks): saved = savedRef.tasks[T], remote = incoming T<br/>canonical(saved) !== canonical(remote)
        TabB->>TabB: clearEditDraft(T) (localStorage task+T)<br/>dispatch(TASK/CLOSE_EDIT_MODAL) -> editingTaskId / editTaskDraft = null<br/>setEditDiscarded(true)
        TabB->>TabB: savedRef, lastSyncedRef = board, dispatch(BOARD/SYNC)
        TabB->>TabB: BoardView: modal closed while URL is /dashboard/task/:id<br/>-> navigate("/dashboard", replace)
        TabB-->>User: EditDiscardedAlert "This task was changed elsewhere."
        Note over TabB,KV: Tab A's PATCH then bumps board_rev, and the SSE refetch in tab B matches savedRef (nothing more to do).
        Note over TabB: The modal stays open when: a different task was saved, tab A's save didn't change T (canonical compare),<br/>or T was deleted elsewhere (saveEdit then adds it back at the end of its cell).
        %% KNOWN RACE (unfixed): the same broadcast race as in section 1, seen from a modal save.
        %% If tab B saves T and the save is still on its 500ms timer when tab A's broadcast arrives,
        %% tab B's save is dropped with no notice. SAVE_EDIT already closed the modal, so
        %% closeStaleEdit can't show EditDiscardedAlert either.
        Note over TabA,TabB: RACE: tab B presses Save before the message arrives. Its modal is already closed (editingTaskId = null),<br/>so closeStaleEdit does nothing. If tab B's save is still on its 500ms timer, tab A's broadcast drops it with no notice (see 1).<br/>If both PATCHes are sent, the second to land gets a 409, and mergeFromServer keeps the server's T and shows SaveConflictAlert.
    end

    rect rgba(240, 38, 38, 0.12)
        Note over User,CLI: 3. The CLI saves a task that a browser tab has open, with unsaved edits, in its modal
        User->>TabB: open task T, type edits (editTaskDraft only, T's versionstamp unchanged)
        User->>CLI: kanby task edit --id T
        CLI->>CliAPI: GET /api/v1/tasks/T
        CliAPI-->>CLI: 200 taskView + ETag v1 (T's versionstamp)
        User->>CLI: answer prompts, confirm Save
        CLI->>CliAPI: PATCH /api/v1/tasks/T {changes} If-Match: v1
        CliAPI->>KV: saveEntity("task", boardId, T, v1)<br/>atomic: check T at v1 + set T + set board_rev
        KV-->>CliAPI: ok, v2
        CliAPI-->>CLI: 200 + ETag v2 -> "Saved task"
        KV-->>Events: board_rev changed
        Events-->>TabB: data: change
        TabB->>TabB: refreshFromServer(), queued on saveChainRef
        alt no edit on the 500ms timer
            TabB->>BoardAPI: GET /api/v1/board
            BoardAPI-->>TabB: 200 board + ETag -> revRef
            TabB->>TabB: diffBoard(savedRef, remote) differs<br/>closeStaleEdit: savedRef's T !== the CLI's T<br/>-> clearEditDraft(T), TASK/CLOSE_EDIT_MODAL, setEditDiscarded(true)
            TabB->>TabB: savedRef = remote, lastSyncedRef = board, dispatch(BOARD/SYNC)<br/>BoardView navigate("/dashboard", replace)
            TabB-->>User: EditDiscardedAlert, the card shows the CLI's version
        else an edit is on the timer (savePendingRef)
            TabB->>TabB: refreshQueuedRef = true (refresh runs after that save)
            TabB->>BoardAPI: that save's PATCH, If-Match: stale revRef
            BoardAPI-->>TabB: 409 {conflict: true}
            TabB->>TabB: mergeFromServer: GET board, closeStaleEdit(remote.tasks) (same close + alert as above)<br/>mergeConflict keeps this tab's changes to entities the CLI didn't touch
        end
        %% KNOWN RACE (unfixed): saving the modal just after the CLI saved the same task shows
        %% SaveConflictAlert, not EditDiscardedAlert.
        %% Where: useBoardPersistence.ts. TASK/SAVE_EDIT nulls editingTaskId before the SSE refetch,
        %% so closeStaleEdit (in refreshFromServer and mergeFromServer) returns early.
        %% Effect: the browser's edits are lost. The 409 merge keeps the CLI's version, and the user
        %% gets the generic conflict notice instead of the "changed elsewhere" one.
        %% Covered by board-save-conflict.spec.ts "a task changed on both sides keeps the CLI's version, with a notice".
        Note over TabB,CLI: RACE: the user presses Save in the modal before the SSE refetch lands. SAVE_EDIT closes the modal, so<br/>closeStaleEdit has nothing to close. The autosave PATCH carries the stale revRef and gets a 409. mergeConflict sees T changed<br/>on both sides and keeps the CLI's version. The browser's edits are lost, with SaveConflictAlert instead of EditDiscardedAlert.<br/>(Playwright: board-save-conflict.spec.ts "a task changed on both sides keeps the CLI's version, with a notice")
    end

    rect rgba(38, 240, 58, 0.15)
        Note over User,CLI: 4. A task or row saved in the CLI shows up in every open browser tab, on any device
        alt kanby row edit / task edit (checked)
            CLI->>CliAPI: PATCH /api/v1/rows/:id or /api/v1/tasks/:id, If-Match: entity versionstamp
            CliAPI->>KV: saveEntity(kind, boardId, entity, expected)<br/>atomic: check entity + set entity + set board_rev
        else kanby row create / task create (unchecked)
            CLI->>CliAPI: POST /api/v1/rows or /api/v1/tasks
            CliAPI->>KV: applyBoardChanges(boardId, {upserts}) with no checks<br/>(rows POST also writes the default columns if the board has none)<br/>atomic: set entities + set board_rev
        end
        KV-->>CliAPI: ok
        CliAPI-->>CLI: 200 / 201
        KV-->>Events: board_rev changed (one kv.watch per open tab)
        Events-->>TabA: data: change
        Events-->>TabB: data: change
        TabB->>BoardAPI: refreshFromServer -> GET /api/v1/board
        BoardAPI-->>TabB: 200 board + ETag
        TabB->>TabB: revRef = ETag, savedRef = remote, lastSyncedRef = board<br/>dispatch(BOARD/SYNC) -> RowSection (row title / color) and TaskCard re-render
        Note over TabA: Tab A does the same, from its own SSE stream. The BroadcastChannel isn't involved:<br/>a refresh sets lastSyncedRef, so nothing is saved or broadcast back.
        Note over Events,TabB: A dropped stream reopens by itself. kv.watch sends the current board_rev on connect,<br/>so the tab refetches and picks up any writes it missed. Pending local edits defer the refresh (see 3).
    end

    rect rgba(160, 38, 240, 0.12)
        Note over User,CLI: 5. The CLI has a task open while a browser saves it: the CLI save gets a 409
        User->>CLI: kanby task edit --id T
        CLI->>CliAPI: GET /api/v1/tasks/T
        CliAPI-->>CLI: 200 + ETag v1 (no lock is held while the user answers prompts)
        User->>TabB: change task T (modal save, drag to another cell, checklist toggle, ...)
        TabB->>BoardAPI: autosave PATCH /api/v1/board {upserts: [T]} If-Match: revRef
        BoardAPI->>KV: applyBoardChanges: set ["task", boardId, T] + set board_rev
        KV-->>BoardAPI: ok (T's versionstamp is now v2)
        User->>CLI: finish prompts, confirm Save
        CLI->>CliAPI: PATCH /api/v1/tasks/T {changes} If-Match: v1
        CliAPI->>KV: findTask again (T now in Trash -> 409 "Restore it in the web app first", deleted -> 404)<br/>validateFields, checkTaskRefs (422)
        CliAPI->>KV: saveEntity("task", boardId, T, v1)<br/>atomic: check T at v1 + set T + set board_rev
        KV--xCliAPI: check failed (T is at v2), nothing written
        CliAPI--xCLI: 409 "This task changed since it was read."
        CLI-->>User: "This task changed while you were editing.<br/>Re-run kanby task edit --id {shortId}." (the prompt answers are lost)
        Note over TabB,CLI: Only a write to T itself blocks the CLI. The browser's autosave upserts just the entities whose JSON changed<br/>(diffBoard), so opening T in a modal or saving other tasks or rows doesn't. The check and the write are one atomic<br/>commit, with no gap between them. The same applies to kanby row edit (row versionstamp) and to two CLI sessions.
    end
